<title>USA: Apartment Investment completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Apartment Investment completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apartment Investment and Management Co said Friday that it completed the previously announced acquisition of general and limited partnership interests in 86,387 apartment units for $54.8 million in cash and warrants.</p>
<p>The warrants allow for the purchase of 399,999 of its shares at an exercise price of $36 per share.</p>
<p>The company said the units are in 540 conventional and affordable apartment communities.</p>
<p>As part of the deal, the company said it also purchased a captive insurance company and other related assets.  </p>
<p>A captive insurance company is one formed to insure the risks of its parent company.</p>
</text>
